comment_data.body:
I'm not 100% sure I understand all the rules, but I think it could be made more clear with something like:
```c
#define CHOMP_PATHSEP(ptr) \
  do { \
    if (!vim_ispathsep_nocolon(*ptr)) { \
      return false; \
    } \
    ptr++; \
  } while (0)

  CHOMP_PATHSEP(p);
  CHOMP_PATHSEP(p);
```
You may need to add a length check in the macro. Then you could do something similar for reading the server name/path:
```c
while (p < end && !vim_ispathsep_nocolon(*p)) {
  CHOMP_SERVER_CHAR(p);
}
```
Just giving some ideas :) Take them or leave them.

